today with some meaty policy we have so much

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.050
to talk about today.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.019
California recall is tonight will be streaming
results live.

00:00:09.019 --> 00:00:10.519
We have a new tax proposal.

00:00:10.519 --> 00:00:12.719
We have new anti-tax mania.

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:14.040
We have all sorts of different things.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:20.720
But let's start with some policy material
from the Democratic Party.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:29.080
Democrats are seeking to increase the corporate
tax as well as income tax on the wealthy to

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:35.950
pay for this three point five trillion dollar
plan about which Joe Manchin is talking, et

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:36.950
cetera, et cetera.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.720
So let's start with a report from the Associated
Press about the proposal.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.699
We will then look at it item by item, and
then we will then look at some of the I guess

00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:53.270
I would call it hyperbolic, panicked reporting
about if you make five million and live in

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.820
NYC, you'll pay 60 percent total.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.910
OK, so we'll go through it piece by piece.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.949
That's the way we like to do it.

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:05.439
House Democrats unveiled a sweeping proposal
yesterday for tax hikes on big corporations

00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:11.090
and the wealthy to fund Joe Biden's three
point five trillion dollar plan.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:15.560
The proposed top tax rate would revert to
thirty nine point six percent on individuals

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.380
earning more than 400000 or 450.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:22.130
For couples, there would be a three percent
tax on wealthier Americans, with adjusted

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.329
income beyond five million a year for big
businesses.

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:29.120
The proposal would lift the corporate tax
rate from twenty one to twenty six point five

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:34.880
percent on incomes beyond five million, slightly
less than the 28 percent rate the president

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.670
had sought in all.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:41.490
The tax hikes are in line with Biden's own
proposals and would bring about the most substantive

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:46.810
changes in the tax code since Republicans
with then-President Donald Trump slashed taxes

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:47.810
in 2017.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.750
Seventeen business and anti-tax groups are
sure to object.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.750
But Democrats are pressing forward.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.009
All right.

00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:56.990
So where do we start?

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:02.380
Well, what are the main provisions of the
bill and how do they change from what we currently

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.380
have?

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.380
So let's look at it.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.689
The top tax bracket would increase on individuals.

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:14.670
The top top tax bracket would increase from
37 percent to thirty nine point six percent.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:19.410
This is that infamous two point six percent
difference that Democrats and Republicans

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.940
have been arguing about for a long time.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:29.650
Remember going from 37 to thirty nine point
six, that's back to the pre Bush top bracket.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:35.270
Before Bush, the top tax rate was thirty nine
point six percent under Clinton, Bush lowered

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.050
it to thirty seven.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.830
Obama let it go back up to thirty nine point
six.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.050
Trump went back down to 37 seven.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.540
That's the scope here.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:50.560
OK, it's a two point six percentage point
gap that is the subject of the argument and

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:51.560
the debate.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.290
Now, this the wording has been muddy and it's
already been changed.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.590
The bracket would start lower.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:02:59.780
Right now.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:05.200
That top tax bracket doesn't kick in until
a couple makes six hundred and twenty eight

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.850
thousand a year together.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:12.720
It appears as though under the Biden plan,
under the Democratic plan, sorry, the House

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.470
Democrats plan that bracket would start lower
at four hundred and fifty thousand dollars

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.010
in joint income per year.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:25.860
OK, there would be a three percent tax on
incomes over five million dollars a year.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:31.370
OK, now it's you know, with all of these things,
there's always a question of how much are

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.560
you capturing by doing this?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:40.320
There is an argument to be made that a lot
of people who make a ton of money are not

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:47.610
taking a salary above five million dollars
a year, that a lot of that would be in stock

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:53.100
options or in other types of deferred compensation,
and it would avoid that three percent tax.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.890
But OK, we'll deal with that eventually.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:04:02.690
Three percent tax on incomes over five million
a year and a corporate tax increase from twenty

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:10.080
one percent to twenty six and a half percent
only on incomes beyond five million dollars.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:19.489
Now, remember, this doesn't apply to so many
corporations, LLC S. S corporations, et cetera,

00:04:19.489 --> 00:04:25.380
because those are what are called pass through
entities and the income is taxed by the individual

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.380
stakeholders on their personal income taxes.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:33.730
So this would apply to a small portion of
corporations.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:40.210
And remember, if you're currently avoiding
a twenty one percent tax rate, you would then

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:47.310
just go to avoiding a 26 and a half percent
tax rate unless we put in place a corporate

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.120
minimum tax or some other mechanisms.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:55.100
Another issue that we've talked about many
times, the estimates are this would raise

00:04:55.100 --> 00:05:00.180
about two point nine dollars trillion dollars
of the three point five trillion dollars that

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.890
the legislation that is being discussed would
cost.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.230
All right.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:09.840
Now, there are some headlines that have been
floating about, you know, in some states and

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:15.870
some cities with this proposal, individuals
who make a lot of money could end up paying

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:16.870
around 60 percent.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:22.630
For example, there's a CNBC, CNBC article
which says top earning New Yorkers that the

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:28.440
New York City could face a sixty one point
two percent combined tax rate.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:33.370
Under the House plan, Californians could be
paying a 59 percent rate.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.370
How could this be?

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.370
Well, let's go through it.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:39.010
First of all, you would have to be at the
top level, OK?

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:42.830
You'd have to be at that five million a year
level.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:47.800
And by the way, if you're at five million
a year, you actually don't pay the three percent

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:48.800
surcharge.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.510
But let's because it starts at five million.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.320
But you could be in New York City, right?

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.160
You pay thirty nine point six percent on income.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:02.570
It's a marginal tax rate, three percent surcharge,
three point eight percent net investment income

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:03.570
tax.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:05.290
That would get you to forty six point four.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:09.740
And then if you're in New York City, you could
have a combined state income tax and city

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.700
income tax of fourteen point eight.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.940
You combine the 46 and the 14 and it's sixty
one point two.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:19.590
Now, that's not your effective tax rate because
remember, these are marginal tax rate.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:23.390
It doesn't account for the standard deduction,
other ways to reduce tax liability.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:27.330
But that's where they're getting sixty one
point two is an exaggerated.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.330
Yes.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:32.940
Are people who make that much probably going
to pay a lot more if this passes?

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:35.110
Yeah, they probably will.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:42.350
But remember, the unless you're really bad
with money, when you make more and more money,

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.750
you're spending a smaller and smaller share
of your income.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.860
I've said before, I'm very conservative financially.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.690
I save the vast majority of my income.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:53.850
I don't spend it.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.010
I live well below my means.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:07:03.490
So if my income tax went up to three or four
points, I'm saving less.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:06.800
It's not actually affecting my day to day
budget.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:10.380
And it's important to understand that at these
super high levels, if you're making 20 million

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:17.670
a year, unless you're doing really bad financial
things, you're not even going to feel this.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:21.470
Now, you can still argue that it's too high
or it's that's a different argument.

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:25.630
But the argument that, you know, the vast
majority of people that are going to be affected

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:29.620
by this should not be spending anywhere near
what they make.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.560
Still can debate whether this is, quote, right.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.470
OK, California, similar example.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:38.860
You could have that forty six point four total
federal and then thirteen point three state.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:41.450
That would get you to fifty nine point seven
in New Jersey.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.290
You could end up at fifty seven point two.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.560
Hawaii, fifty seven point four.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:51.540
One other issue is we don't know whether the
limit on salt state and local tax deductions

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:54.100
is going to be removed.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.420
This is just a proposal.

00:07:56.420 --> 00:08:00.750
And for people saying this is too high, people
are going to move out of New York City, they're

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:04.270
going to move out of California, the market
will tell us, you know, if it passes and people

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:06.760
start leaving New York City in California.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:11.070
At higher rates than people generally move
in and out, then it will be a sign that it's

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.070
too high.

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:16.150
And remember that even if people move out
the state but I'm sorry, the federal government

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:19.550
or even the state, depending on, you know,
what's going on, they could end up with more

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:27.130
money because there is taxation is sort of
on a curve and you could raise taxes and push

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:31.840
out taxpayers, but still take in more money
in total.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:36.070
That's a that's just a broad, you know, macroeconomic
taxation concept here.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:40.810
We're talking about federal, though, and important
that this does nothing about the multinationals

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:45.890
that can use different accounting tricks to
book revenue and profit in different countries

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:49.440
and to end up losing money on paper in the
United States.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.480
This won't change that.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:52.770
